notes={'00732':['Monotherapy requires EGFR-expressing RAS wild-type mCRC after oxaliplatin- and irinotecan-based therapy failure with irinotecan intolerance; it is not unrestricted first-line monotherapy.','Severe skin recurrence requires recovery within the maximum two-week interruption and review of the actual previous dose; no automatic re-escalation.'],'00585':['Full resolution of treatment-related diarrhoea is required before irinotecan. Current grade 2–4 diarrhoea holds and dose history must be assessed component by component.'],'00733':['Do not substitute the 00447 renal policy: this NCCP source permits specialist consideration of 50% oxaliplatin for CrCl below 30 mL/min or haemodialysis, whereas 00447 lists contraindication below 30 mL/min. The decision requires the source-specific renal and clinical review.'],'00447':['This NCCP source lists renal and hepatic impairment as baseline exclusions and contraindicates oxaliplatin below 30 mL/min. Do not copy the separate 00733 50% option.','The PRIME trial tested panitumumab with FOLFOX4, not this exact modified FOLFOX6 administration schedule.'],'00448':['First-line RAS wild-type mCRC or second-line after fluoropyrimidine-based chemotherapy excluding irinotecan; distinguish trial population and current indication.','Complete irinotecan diarrhoea recovery and actual dose history remain required, even where a table gives a grade boundary.'],'00551':['NCCP 00551c is previously treated MSI-H/dMMR colorectal cancer. The v7a continuation paragraph differs from RCC/melanoma and from 00900: do not silently substitute a 480 mg IV every 28 days continuation option from adjacent indications. Review source switching-language ambiguity with the consultant/pharmacist.'],'00900':['This flat-dose nivolumab 240 mg combination protocol has its own colorectal indication, four 21-day combination cycles and continuation options. Do not treat the weight-based 00551 protocol as interchangeable.'],'00890':['Use the current v2a fruquintinib liver/proteinuria/HTN/skin pathways. Dose floors, recurrence handling and monitoring differ from regorafenib.']}
notes['00551'] += ['NCCP 00551c eligibility includes ECOG 0–2, unlike 00900 ECOG 0–1. Dose-modification toxicity grading uses CTCAE v4. See NCCP pages 5–10.','Grade 3 colitis requires permanent discontinuation, including nivolumab monotherapy after the combination. Apply the source-specific endocrine exceptions: symptomatic grade 2/3 thyroid dysfunction or hypophysitis requires withholding, while an asymptomatic patient on replacement may continue; adrenal insufficiency grade 2 requires withholding and grade 3/4 requires discontinuation.','Hepatic impairment: source caution for moderate/severe impairment must not be replaced with the different 00900 Table 2 wording.']
notes['00900'] += ['NCCP 00900 eligibility includes ECOG 0–1; toxicity dose-modification grading uses CTCAE v4. Treatment duration is up to 24 months. See NCCP pages 1–6.','Grade 3 colitis requires permanent discontinuation, including after transition to nivolumab alone. Symptomatic grade 2/3 thyroid dysfunction or hypophysitis requires withholding; asymptomatic replacement-only conditions have specific continuation exceptions. Adrenal insufficiency grade 2 requires withholding and grade 3/4 requires discontinuation.','NCCP Table 2 states no hepatic adjustment for mild/moderate impairment and none expected for severe impairment; distinguish this organ-impairment guidance from immune hepatitis and from the separate 00551 caution.']
notes['00890'] += ['NCCP pages 3–4: proteinuria at least 2 g/24 h requires withholding; restart requires full resolution or less than 1 g/24 h. Do not substitute another VEGF inhibitor’s threshold.','Palmar-plantar erythrodysaesthesia grade 2 resumes at the same dose after specified recovery; grade 3 resumes at a reduced dose. Dose levels are 5 mg, 4 mg and 3 mg daily; inability to tolerate 3 mg requires discontinuation.','Other grade 4 toxicities require discontinuation, with the source-described consultant rechallenge exception considered separately; this exception does not override organ-specific permanent-stop pathways.','EMA Fruzaqla sections 4.4/4.5: gastrointestinal perforation requires permanent discontinuation; PRES requires discontinuation; suspected arterial thrombosis requires immediate discontinuation. Do not import a blanket permanent-stop rule for every fistula from another regimen.','EMA surgical precautions: withhold for at least two weeks before major surgery; do not restart for at least two weeks afterwards and until adequate healing. Avoid strong or moderate CYP3A inducers.']
